    "result_text": "Everything passes \u2014 the project has one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, keeping the existing `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` fields.\n\nTo keep logic where it belongs and avoid duplication, I:\n\n1. **Extracted the membership-number formatting** out of `OwnerMapper.formatMembershipNumber` into a new model class `model/MembershipNumber.java` with a static `forOwner(owner)` method \u2014 matching the existing idiom of `CheckDigit`, `ContactPreference`, and `AgeBand`. This makes the format reusable rather than trapped in the mapper.\n\n2. **Updated `OwnerMapper`** to call `MembershipNumber.forOwner(owner)`, removing the now-redundant protected method.\n\n3. **Enriched `OwnerAuditLogger`** to reuse the existing `MembershipLevelEvaluator` (injected via constructor) for `membershipLevel` and the new `MembershipNumber.forOwner(owner)` for `membershipNumber` \u2014 no logic was copied. The audit logger stays a thin single-responsibility component; the derivation logic lives in its owning units.\n\nVerified output: `AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-21 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`, and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
